Comment: The schedulers, their BPF programs and the scx_utils, scx_stats,
 scx_arena and scx_cargo libraries are GPL-2.0-only. The BPF headers
 from the kernel (scheds/include) are GPL-2.0-only WITH
 Linux-syscall-note or LGPL-2.1 OR BSD-2-Clause, as each file says.

Files: upstream/scx-vendor-*.tar.xz
Copyright: the authors of each crate, as listed in its Cargo.toml
License: Expat or Apache-2.0
Comment: Most crates are "MIT OR Apache-2.0" or MIT. The others:
  libbpf-sys (the libbpf 1.7.0 linked in statically)  BSD-2-Clause, its
    libbpf source LGPL-2.1 OR BSD-2-Clause
  libbpf-rs, libbpf-cargo, libarena-rs  LGPL-2.1-only OR BSD-2-Clause
  bindgen  BSD-3-Clause
  clang-sys  Apache-2.0
  libloading  ISC
  colored  MPL-2.0
  clap_main  GPL-3.0-only; a procedural macro run by the compiler, it
    writes the few lines that parse scx_lavd's arguments
  memchr, aho-corasick and a few others  Unlicense OR MIT
  unicode-ident  (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0
 The full text of each licence is in the crate's folder in the crates
 tarball.

